      "text": " hide thousands of machine instructions, and the compiler is the machine that performs that hiding.\n\nThis is the story of how that machine works.\n\n## 1.1 What a compiler actually does\n\nA compiler is a program that reads one program and produces another. The input is source code written in a high-level language. The output is machine code that a processor can execute. In between, the compiler performs a sequence of transformations, each one taking the program from one representation to another.\n\nThe overall shape of a modern compiler looks like this:\n\n```text\nSource code\n    |\n    v\n[ Front End ]\n",
