      "text": " hide thousands of machine instructions, and the compiler is the machine that performs that hiding.\n\nThis book is about that machine. It is a tour of the ideas that make modern compilers possible, told through the lens of a single language, a small but complete one called Tiny. Tiny is not a toy. It has functions, closures, objects, exceptions, and a type system. It is just small enough that you can hold the whole thing in your head, which is the point.\n\nThe tour has three parts. The first is the theory: the mathematical foundations that make compilation a science rather than an art. The second is the practice",
